{"call_id":"73164c08-2e1b-4d0e-b31c-16a4acc982e4","metadata":{"error_type":null,"finish_reason":"stop","mode":"ok","response_id":"b3a023f21bbaf4b0c1b1c4340e50f8e7.73163fe57870ed40bf6b7b1893539e4d","status_code":null,"stop_reason":null,"usage":{"cached_tokens":256,"completion_tokens":3415,"completion_tokens_details":{"accepted_prediction_tokens":null,"audio_tokens":null,"reasoning_tokens":0,"rejected_prediction_tokens":null,"text_tokens":null},"prompt_tokens":17267,"prompt_tokens_details":{"audio_tokens":null,"cache_write_tokens":null,"cached_tokens":256,"image_tokens":null,"text_tokens":null},"total_tokens":20682}},"raw_response":{"choices":[{"finish_reason":"stop","index":0,"logprobs":null,"message":{"annotations":null,"audio":null,"content":"{\"protocol_version\":\"impact-response-v5\",\"action\":\"finish\",\"unit_outcome\":\"analyzed\",\"candidates\":[{\"rule_ref\":\"R1\",\"case_impacts\":[{\"case_ref\":\"C1\",\"level\":\"none\",\"reason\":\"该用例的验证目标与执行步骤均不涉及订单保留期或超期查询返回码；保留期参数变化对此用例无直接影响。\",\"citations\":[\"F6\",\"F26\"],\"verification_points\":[]}]},{\"rule_ref\":\"R2\",\"case_impacts\":[{\"case_ref\":\"C1\",\"level\":\"major\",\"reason\":\"该用例的核心目标与关键执行步骤均围绕被删除的优惠码规则展开，并包含对应折扣预期；新版文档整节删除后，该用例失去需求依据，仅作为停用候选提交评审。\",\"citations\":[\"F6\",\"F23\",\"F24\",\"F25\",\"F26\"],\"verification_points\":[\"确认优惠码折扣行为是否由替代规则覆盖\",\"如确认删除，按停用候选提交评审，不直接推断已生效或全面停用\"]}]},{\"rule_ref\":\"R3\",\"case_impacts\":[{\"case_ref\":\"C1\",\"level\":\"none\",\"reason\":\"新增订单导出接口规则与该用例现有验证目标及步骤无关，不产生直接影响。\",\"citations\":[\"F6\",\"F23\"],\"verification_points\":[]}]}],\"evidence_outcomes\":[],\"summary\":\"已完成用例C1对规则R1、R2、R3的影响分析：R2删除优惠码规则直接影响该用例，标记为重大影响并建议停用候选；R1与R3与该用例验证目标无关。\",\"unresolved\":[\"目标发布/部署状态仅有用户声明，缺少部署证据；R2/R3的实际生效状态未知。\",\"R2删除后未提供替代规则；仅提出停用候选，不做全面停用项目推断。\",\"用例执行说明提示存在刻意缺失的负向条件，现有证据不足以推断其具体内容，需保留待评审确认。\"]}","function_call":null,"reasoning":"The user wants me to analyze document impact for a specific case (C1) based on the provided large JSON context. According to the instructions, this is the \"case_impacts\" stage.\n\nKey instructions from protocol:\n- Return one impact-response-v5 JSON object.\n- Current coordination stage is \"case_impacts\".\n- For finish, unit_outcome must be analyzed or evidence_insufficient, never null, and reads empty.\n- Case stage: assess every R rule for the current complete case identified by primary_ref, using its entire JSON, execution_notes, original sources and rule evidence.\n- Return rule_ref/case_impacts for that current case; evidence_outcomes is empty.\n- Other cases may be read as supplementary evidence, but each has its own analysis task; do not turn this call into whole-project coverage.\n- Case citations are F strings from fixed_case_evidence for the stated case_ref.\n- Each F selects a literal field path in the complete JSON or execution_notes; values are already in those complete reads.\n- The server binds T/F selections to exact original positions/versions/paths/values and verifies them.\n- For read request only needed fixed P/S/C/D reads with no candidates, evidence_outcomes or outcome.\n- Other catalogs are retrieval metadata, not supplied evidence.\n- Preserve deliberate negative conditions.\n- Report missing evidence explicitly.\n- All proposals pending review, deployment unknown.\n- Do not execute tests or change official records.\n\nThe primary case is C1 (case_id: 0665f18f-067e-4964-92e4-2ad52b65ed5b). Rules are R1, R2, R3 corresponding to the three candidates from discovery.\n\nR1: order_retention_period_extended (order retention changed from 7 to 9 days)\nR2: promo_code_promo5_discount_removed (promo code rule removed)\nR3: order_export_endpoint_added (new export endpoint added)\n\nCase C1 content_json:\n- objective: \"验证有效优惠码减5元\"\n- extension: {\"false\": false, \"null\": null, \"zero\": 0}\n- steps: 8 steps, mostly \"记录受控环境信息1\" through \"记录受控环境信息7\", then step 7: action \"使用PROMO5创建订单\", expected {\"discount\": 5}\n- execution_notes: \"阅读所有步骤，保留刻意缺失的负向条件。\"\n- source_refs point to old document version (v1) which had the promo code section.\n\nNeed to assess impact of each rule on case C1.\n\nFor R2 (promo code removed): This rule is directly about the promo code section that is absent in new version. The case C1 objective is \"验证有效优惠码减5元\" and step 7 uses PROMO5 and expects discount 5. Since the rule was removed, this case is directly impacted. The impact level should be \"major\" because the requirement basis for the test case is deleted. But since it's a deletion, the case might need to be disabled or reviewed. The protocol says \"deletion only propose disable candidate\". For case impact level: \"none\", \"minor\", \"major\", \"uncertain\". Major seems appropriate.\n\nCitations: Need F refs from fixed_case_evidence for case_ref C1. The fixed_case_evidence maps F keys to paths.\n- F6: objective -> \"验证有效优惠码减5元\"\n- F23: steps[7].action -> \"使用PROMO5创建订单\"\n- F24: steps[7].expected -> {\"discount\":5}\n- F25: steps[7].expected.discount -> 5\n- F26: execution_notes -> \"阅读所有步骤，保留刻意缺失的负向条件。\"\n\nAlso could cite source refs? No, citations are F strings from fixed_case_evidence. Document citations are T strings but those are for rules. For case impact, we use citations from F.\n\nFor R1 (retention period extended 7->9 days): Case C1 does not seem related to order retention. It's about promo code. So impact level \"none\". Need reason and citations? For none, the CaseAnchoredCandidate schema requires case_ref, level, reason, citations (minItems 1). So even for none, citations are required. We can cite F6 or F26 maybe? Or F8-F22 (generic environment info steps). But we should cite something that shows the case doesn't test retention. Maybe F6 (objective) and F7-F22 (steps) or just F6 and F23. But citations min 1. For none, we can cite F6 (objective shows it's about promo code, not retention). Also maybe F26 (execution notes). Let's pick F6 and F26.\n\nFor R3 (order export added): Case C1 is about promo code, not export. Impact level \"none\". Cite F6, maybe F23.\n\nNeed to return rule_ref for each rule. The rules array has R1, R2, R3. We need one CaseAnchoredRuleAssessment per rule.\n\nCaseAnchoredRuleAssessment:\n- rule_ref: string pattern ^R[1-9][0-9]*$\n- case_impacts: array of CaseAnchoredCandidate, minItems 1.\n\nSo for R1:\n- case_ref: \"C1\"\n- level: \"none\"\n- reason: explain retention change does not affect this case which verifies promo code discount, citing objective and notes.\n- citations: [\"F6\", \"F26\"] or just [\"F6\"]. Let's include F6 and F23 maybe. But for none, one is enough. I'll use [\"F6\", \"F26\"].\n- verification_points: optional. Maybe empty or include \"No retention operations or 410 conditions present in case steps.\" The schema doesn't require it.\n\nFor R2:\n- case_ref: \"C1\"\n- level: \"major\"\n- reason: The case objective and step 7 directly depend on the removed promo code rule. The new version deleted the entire 优惠码 section, so the requirement basis for this test case no longer exists. Pending review; deletion only proposes disable candidate.\n- citations: [\"F6\", \"F23\", \"F24\", \"F25\", \"F26\"]\n- verification_points: maybe [\"Confirm whether PROMO5 discount behavior still exists under a revised requirement\", \"If rule deletion is confirmed, propose case disable/decommission pending review\"].\n- applicability_suggestion? This is in RuleCandidate, not in CaseAnchoredCandidate. Not needed here.\n\nFor R3:\n- case_ref: \"C1\"\n- level: \"none\"\n- reason: New export endpoint rule does not relate to promo code discount verification in this case.\n- citations: [\"F6\", \"F23\"]\n- verification_points: optional.\n\nNeed to ensure evidence_outcomes is empty for case stage.\naction: \"finish\" because we are finishing.\nunit_outcome: \"analyzed\" because we assessed all rules.\nreads: empty (must be empty for finish).\nsummary: Chinese text summarizing the impact analysis for case C1.\nunresolved: Include relevant unresolved items from context? The instruction says report missing evidence explicitly. We can include:\n- \"Target release/deployment status remains user-declared without deployment evidence; applicability of R2/R3 changes is unknown.\"\n- \"For R2, no replacement rule for PROMO5 discount is supplied; deletion is a disable candidate pending review only.\"\n- \"Case C1 contains deliberate missing negative conditions (execution_notes F26); these cannot be inferred from promo code rule deletion alone.\" Wait, the execution notes say \"阅读所有步骤，保留刻意缺失的负向条件。\" It says preserve deliberate negative conditions. But the steps have no explicit negative conditions visible except maybe the extension object has false/null/zero keys. Actually the case has extension {false:false,null:null,zero:0}. This might represent negative conditions? The execution notes mention \"保留刻意缺失的负向条件\". So there are negative conditions that are deliberately missing. We should not infer them. It's fine.\n\nNeed to make sure all citations correspond to fixed_case_evidence for C1. F refs are defined. F1-F26 are available. We can only use F1-F26. Good.\n\nPotential issue: The protocol says \"Case citations are F strings from fixed_case_evidence for the stated case_ref. Each F selects a literal field path in the complete JSON or execution_notes; values are already in those complete reads. Do not output paths, values, UUIDs or hashes. Case metadata titles are not content_json fields.\"\n\nSo in reason strings, we should not mention path strings like \"objective\" maybe? It says do not output paths, values, UUIDs or hashes. That means in the JSON output, we should not include literal JSON paths or values as raw text? Or does it mean we should not output them in the fields where not needed? The instruction \"Do not output paths, values, UUIDs or hashes\" likely means in the reason text, don't quote the exact values/paths/UUIDs/hashes. Because the server binds T/F selections to exact values. So we should avoid including the literal text of the values in the reason. Instead we can describe them generically.\n\nFor example, for R2 reason, instead of writing: \"objective is '验证有效优惠码减5元' and step 7 action is '使用PROMO5创建订单'\" we should write something like \"用例目标与关键步骤直接围绕被删除的优惠码规则构建，依赖该规则的折扣预期\" or similar. But is \"优惠码\" a value from the document? Yes, but it's also a rule summary. The candidate summary already has text. However the instruction is strong: \"Do not output paths, values, UUIDs or hashes.\" I think it means don't include actual field paths (like steps[7]) or the actual values (like \"使用PROMO5创建订单\") because they are in F citations. We can refer to them via F citations. But it's okay to describe generally.\n\nLet's read the protocol carefully: \"Case citations are F strings from fixed_case_evidence for the stated case_ref. Each F selects a literal field path in the complete JSON or execution_notes; values are already in those complete reads. Do not output paths, values, UUIDs or hashes.\"\n\nSo in the JSON output, we should not include paths or values from the case content. The reason should not contain exact field paths or values. But can it contain document quotes? Document citations are T strings and those are selected separately. The rule summaries already have document quotes. But in case impact reason, we should avoid duplicating them.\n\nSo for R2 reason: \"该用例的核心目标与关键执行步骤均围绕被删除的优惠码规则展开，且包含该规则对应的折扣预期；在新版文档删除整节依据后，该用例失去需求支撑，建议仅作为停用候选提交评审。\" This avoids quoting paths/values. Good.\n\nFor citations, we reference F numbers, not the values. That's fine.\n\nNeed to ensure JSON schema compliance.\nprotocol_version: \"impact-response-v5\"\naction: \"finish\"\ncandidates: array of CaseAnchoredRuleAssessment objects.\n- rule_ref: \"R1\"\n  case_impacts: [{case_ref:\"C1\", level:\"none\", reason:\"...\", citations:[\"F6\",\"F26\"], verification_points:[]}]\n- rule_ref: \"R2\"\n  case_impacts: [{case_ref:\"C1\", level:\"major\", reason:\"...\", citations:[\"F6\",\"F23\",\"F24\",\"F25\",\"F26\"], verification_points:[\"...\"]}]\n- rule_ref: \"R3\"\n  case_impacts: [{case_ref:\"C1\", level:\"none\", reason:\"...\", citations:[\"F6\",\"F23\"], verification_points:[]}]\n\nevidence_outcomes: []\nsummary: \"已完成用例C1对规则R1、R2、R3的影响分析：R2删除优惠码规则直接影响该用例，标记为重大影响并建议停用候选；R1与R3与该用例验证目标无关。\"\nunit_outcome: \"analyzed\"\nunresolved: [\n\"目标发布/部署状态仅有用户声明，缺少部署证据；R2/R3的实际生效状态未知。\",\n\"R2删除后未提供替代规则；仅提出停用候选，不做全面停用项目推断。\",\n\"用例执行说明提示存在刻意缺失的负向条件，现有证据不足以推断其具体内容，需保留待评审确认。\"\n]\n\nDouble-check if any additional reads needed. The instruction says for read request only needed fixed P/S/C/D reads. But we have all needed. read can be omitted or empty. Schema: reads is optional property inside BoundReadRequest but not required at root? The schema shows reads as a property but not in required. We can omit it. The protocol says for read request only needed... For finish reads empty. So we can omit reads entirely.\n\nConfirm CaseAnchoredRuleAssessment required fields: rule_ref, case_impacts. CaseAnchoredCandidate required: case_ref, level, reason, citations. Good.\n\nNeed to ensure no additionalProperties. So only those fields.\n\nLet's draft final JSON.\n\nOne more thing: The instruction says \"Preserve deliberate negative conditions.\" In case stage, for C1, the execution_notes (F26) mention \"阅读所有步骤，保留刻意缺失的负向条件。\" This means when assessing impact, we should note that negative conditions are deliberately missing and preserved, not infer them. In R2, the impact is major but we should note that. In unresolved we have it.\n\nIs there any need to read other cases (C2, C3)? No, \"Other cases may be read as supplementary evidence, but each has its own analysis task; do not turn this call into whole-project coverage.\" So we don't include them.\n\nIs there any missing evidence? The old source is available. The new source is available. Deploy status unknown. Fine.\n\nLet's produce the JSON.","reasoning_content":"The user wants me to analyze document impact for a specific case (C1) based on the provided large JSON context. According to the instructions, this is the \"case_impacts\" stage.\n\nKey instructions from protocol:\n- Return one impact-response-v5 JSON object.\n- Current coordination stage is \"case_impacts\".\n- For finish, unit_outcome must be analyzed or evidence_insufficient, never null, and reads empty.\n- Case stage: assess every R rule for the current complete case identified by primary_ref, using its entire JSON, execution_notes, original sources and rule evidence.\n- Return rule_ref/case_impacts for that current case; evidence_outcomes is empty.\n- Other cases may be read as supplementary evidence, but each has its own analysis task; do not turn this call into whole-project coverage.\n- Case citations are F strings from fixed_case_evidence for the stated case_ref.\n- Each F selects a literal field path in the complete JSON or execution_notes; values are already in those complete reads.\n- The server binds T/F selections to exact original positions/versions/paths/values and verifies them.\n- For read request only needed fixed P/S/C/D reads with no candidates, evidence_outcomes or outcome.\n- Other catalogs are retrieval metadata, not supplied evidence.\n- Preserve deliberate negative conditions.\n- Report missing evidence explicitly.\n- All proposals pending review, deployment unknown.\n- Do not execute tests or change official records.\n\nThe primary case is C1 (case_id: 0665f18f-067e-4964-92e4-2ad52b65ed5b). Rules are R1, R2, R3 corresponding to the three candidates from discovery.\n\nR1: order_retention_period_extended (order retention changed from 7 to 9 days)\nR2: promo_code_promo5_discount_removed (promo code rule removed)\nR3: order_export_endpoint_added (new export endpoint added)\n\nCase C1 content_json:\n- objective: \"验证有效优惠码减5元\"\n- extension: {\"false\": false, \"null\": null, \"zero\": 0}\n- steps: 8 steps, mostly \"记录受控环境信息1\" through \"记录受控环境信息7\", then step 7: action \"使用PROMO5创建订单\", expected {\"discount\": 5}\n- execution_notes: \"阅读所有步骤，保留刻意缺失的负向条件。\"\n- source_refs point to old document version (v1) which had the promo code section.\n\nNeed to assess impact of each rule on case C1.\n\nFor R2 (promo code removed): This rule is directly about the promo code section that is absent in new version. The case C1 objective is \"验证有效优惠码减5元\" and step 7 uses PROMO5 and expects discount 5. Since the rule was removed, this case is directly impacted. The impact level should be \"major\" because the requirement basis for the test case is deleted. But since it's a deletion, the case might need to be disabled or reviewed. The protocol says \"deletion only propose disable candidate\". For case impact level: \"none\", \"minor\", \"major\", \"uncertain\". Major seems appropriate.\n\nCitations: Need F refs from fixed_case_evidence for case_ref C1. The fixed_case_evidence maps F keys to paths.\n- F6: objective -> \"验证有效优惠码减5元\"\n- F23: steps[7].action -> \"使用PROMO5创建订单\"\n- F24: steps[7].expected -> {\"discount\":5}\n- F25: steps[7].expected.discount -> 5\n- F26: execution_notes -> \"阅读所有步骤，保留刻意缺失的负向条件。\"\n\nAlso could cite source refs? No, citations are F strings from fixed_case_evidence. Document citations are T strings but those are for rules. For case impact, we use citations from F.\n\nFor R1 (retention period extended 7->9 days): Case C1 does not seem related to order retention. It's about promo code. So impact level \"none\". Need reason and citations? For none, the CaseAnchoredCandidate schema requires case_ref, level, reason, citations (minItems 1). So even for none, citations are required. We can cite F6 or F26 maybe? Or F8-F22 (generic environment info steps). But we should cite something that shows the case doesn't test retention. Maybe F6 (objective) and F7-F22 (steps) or just F6 and F23. But citations min 1. For none, we can cite F6 (objective shows it's about promo code, not retention). Also maybe F26 (execution notes). Let's pick F6 and F26.\n\nFor R3 (order export added): Case C1 is about promo code, not export. Impact level \"none\". Cite F6, maybe F23.\n\nNeed to return rule_ref for each rule. The rules array has R1, R2, R3. We need one CaseAnchoredRuleAssessment per rule.\n\nCaseAnchoredRuleAssessment:\n- rule_ref: string pattern ^R[1-9][0-9]*$\n- case_impacts: array of CaseAnchoredCandidate, minItems 1.\n\nSo for R1:\n- case_ref: \"C1\"\n- level: \"none\"\n- reason: explain retention change does not affect this case which verifies promo code discount, citing objective and notes.\n- citations: [\"F6\", \"F26\"] or just [\"F6\"]. Let's include F6 and F23 maybe. But for none, one is enough. I'll use [\"F6\", \"F26\"].\n- verification_points: optional. Maybe empty or include \"No retention operations or 410 conditions present in case steps.\" The schema doesn't require it.\n\nFor R2:\n- case_ref: \"C1\"\n- level: \"major\"\n- reason: The case objective and step 7 directly depend on the removed promo code rule. The new version deleted the entire 优惠码 section, so the requirement basis for this test case no longer exists. Pending review; deletion only proposes disable candidate.\n- citations: [\"F6\", \"F23\", \"F24\", \"F25\", \"F26\"]\n- verification_points: maybe [\"Confirm whether PROMO5 discount behavior still exists under a revised requirement\", \"If rule deletion is confirmed, propose case disable/decommission pending review\"].\n- applicability_suggestion? This is in RuleCandidate, not in CaseAnchoredCandidate. Not needed here.\n\nFor R3:\n- case_ref: \"C1\"\n- level: \"none\"\n- reason: New export endpoint rule does not relate to promo code discount verification in this case.\n- citations: [\"F6\", \"F23\"]\n- verification_points: optional.\n\nNeed to ensure evidence_outcomes is empty for case stage.\naction: \"finish\" because we are finishing.\nunit_outcome: \"analyzed\" because we assessed all rules.\nreads: empty (must be empty for finish).\nsummary: Chinese text summarizing the impact analysis for case C1.\nunresolved: Include relevant unresolved items from context? The instruction says report missing evidence explicitly. We can include:\n- \"Target release/deployment status remains user-declared without deployment evidence; applicability of R2/R3 changes is unknown.\"\n- \"For R2, no replacement rule for PROMO5 discount is supplied; deletion is a disable candidate pending review only.\"\n- \"Case C1 contains deliberate missing negative conditions (execution_notes F26); these cannot be inferred from promo code rule deletion alone.\" Wait, the execution notes say \"阅读所有步骤，保留刻意缺失的负向条件。\" It says preserve deliberate negative conditions. But the steps have no explicit negative conditions visible except maybe the extension object has false/null/zero keys. Actually the case has extension {false:false,null:null,zero:0}. This might represent negative conditions? The execution notes mention \"保留刻意缺失的负向条件\". So there are negative conditions that are deliberately missing. We should not infer them. It's fine.\n\nNeed to make sure all citations correspond to fixed_case_evidence for C1. F refs are defined. F1-F26 are available. We can only use F1-F26. Good.\n\nPotential issue: The protocol says \"Case citations are F strings from fixed_case_evidence for the stated case_ref. Each F selects a literal field path in the complete JSON or execution_notes; values are already in those complete reads. Do not output paths, values, UUIDs or hashes. Case metadata titles are not content_json fields.\"\n\nSo in reason strings, we should not mention path strings like \"objective\" maybe? It says do not output paths, values, UUIDs or hashes. That means in the JSON output, we should not include literal JSON paths or values as raw text? Or does it mean we should not output them in the fields where not needed? The instruction \"Do not output paths, values, UUIDs or hashes\" likely means in the reason text, don't quote the exact values/paths/UUIDs/hashes. Because the server binds T/F selections to exact values. So we should avoid including the literal text of the values in the reason. Instead we can describe them generically.\n\nFor example, for R2 reason, instead of writing: \"objective is '验证有效优惠码减5元' and step 7 action is '使用PROMO5创建订单'\" we should write something like \"用例目标与关键步骤直接围绕被删除的优惠码规则构建，依赖该规则的折扣预期\" or similar. But is \"优惠码\" a value from the document? Yes, but it's also a rule summary. The candidate summary already has text. However the instruction is strong: \"Do not output paths, values, UUIDs or hashes.\" I think it means don't include actual field paths (like steps[7]) or the actual values (like \"使用PROMO5创建订单\") because they are in F citations. We can refer to them via F citations. But it's okay to describe generally.\n\nLet's read the protocol carefully: \"Case citations are F strings from fixed_case_evidence for the stated case_ref. Each F selects a literal field path in the complete JSON or execution_notes; values are already in those complete reads. Do not output paths, values, UUIDs or hashes.\"\n\nSo in the JSON output, we should not include paths or values from the case content. The reason should not contain exact field paths or values. But can it contain document quotes? Document citations are T strings and those are selected separately. The rule summaries already have document quotes. But in case impact reason, we should avoid duplicating them.\n\nSo for R2 reason: \"该用例的核心目标与关键执行步骤均围绕被删除的优惠码规则展开，且包含该规则对应的折扣预期；在新版文档删除整节依据后，该用例失去需求支撑，建议仅作为停用候选提交评审。\" This avoids quoting paths/values. Good.\n\nFor citations, we reference F numbers, not the values. That's fine.\n\nNeed to ensure JSON schema compliance.\nprotocol_version: \"impact-response-v5\"\naction: \"finish\"\ncandidates: array of CaseAnchoredRuleAssessment objects.\n- rule_ref: \"R1\"\n  case_impacts: [{case_ref:\"C1\", level:\"none\", reason:\"...\", citations:[\"F6\",\"F26\"], verification_points:[]}]\n- rule_ref: \"R2\"\n  case_impacts: [{case_ref:\"C1\", level:\"major\", reason:\"...\", citations:[\"F6\",\"F23\",\"F24\",\"F25\",\"F26\"], verification_points:[\"...\"]}]\n- rule_ref: \"R3\"\n  case_impacts: [{case_ref:\"C1\", level:\"none\", reason:\"...\", citations:[\"F6\",\"F23\"], verification_points:[]}]\n\nevidence_outcomes: []\nsummary: \"已完成用例C1对规则R1、R2、R3的影响分析：R2删除优惠码规则直接影响该用例，标记为重大影响并建议停用候选；R1与R3与该用例验证目标无关。\"\nunit_outcome: \"analyzed\"\nunresolved: [\n\"目标发布/部署状态仅有用户声明，缺少部署证据；R2/R3的实际生效状态未知。\",\n\"R2删除后未提供替代规则；仅提出停用候选，不做全面停用项目推断。\",\n\"用例执行说明提示存在刻意缺失的负向条件，现有证据不足以推断其具体内容，需保留待评审确认。\"\n]\n\nDouble-check if any additional reads needed. The instruction says for read request only needed fixed P/S/C/D reads. But we have all needed. read can be omitted or empty. Schema: reads is optional property inside BoundReadRequest but not required at root? The schema shows reads as a property but not in required. We can omit it. The protocol says for read request only needed... For finish reads empty. So we can omit reads entirely.\n\nConfirm CaseAnchoredRuleAssessment required fields: rule_ref, case_impacts. CaseAnchoredCandidate required: case_ref, level, reason, citations. Good.\n\nNeed to ensure no additionalProperties. So only those fields.\n\nLet's draft final JSON.\n\nOne more thing: The instruction says \"Preserve deliberate negative conditions.\" In case stage, for C1, the execution_notes (F26) mention \"阅读所有步骤，保留刻意缺失的负向条件。\" This means when assessing impact, we should note that negative conditions are deliberately missing and preserved, not infer them. In R2, the impact is major but we should note that. In unresolved we have it.\n\nIs there any need to read other cases (C2, C3)? No, \"Other cases may be read as supplementary evidence, but each has its own analysis task; do not turn this call into whole-project coverage.\" So we don't include them.\n\nIs there any missing evidence? The old source is available. The new source is available. Deploy status unknown. Fine.\n\nLet's produce the JSON.","refusal":null,"role":"assistant","tool_calls":null}}],"created":1791167939,"id":"b3a023f21bbaf4b0c1b1c4340e50f8e7.73163fe57870ed40bf6b7b1893539e4d","metadata":null,"model":"step-5-preview","moderation":null,"object":"chat.completion","service_tier":null,"system_fingerprint":null,"usage":{"cached_tokens":256,"completion_tokens":3415,"completion_tokens_details":{"accepted_prediction_tokens":null,"audio_tokens":null,"reasoning_tokens":0,"rejected_prediction_tokens":null,"text_tokens":null},"prompt_tokens":17267,"prompt_tokens_details":{"audio_tokens":null,"cache_write_tokens":null,"cached_tokens":256,"image_tokens":null,"text_tokens":null},"total_tokens":20682}},"request_sha256":"2056f1c38cbe049f82644af91da93d150912d2f50e7b1e7572d6451bb50b8506","text":"{\"protocol_version\":\"impact-response-v5\",\"action\":\"finish\",\"unit_outcome\":\"analyzed\",\"candidates\":[{\"rule_ref\":\"R1\",\"case_impacts\":[{\"case_ref\":\"C1\",\"level\":\"none\",\"reason\":\"该用例的验证目标与执行步骤均不涉及订单保留期或超期查询返回码；保留期参数变化对此用例无直接影响。\",\"citations\":[\"F6\",\"F26\"],\"verification_points\":[]}]},{\"rule_ref\":\"R2\",\"case_impacts\":[{\"case_ref\":\"C1\",\"level\":\"major\",\"reason\":\"该用例的核心目标与关键执行步骤均围绕被删除的优惠码规则展开，并包含对应折扣预期；新版文档整节删除后，该用例失去需求依据，仅作为停用候选提交评审。\",\"citations\":[\"F6\",\"F23\",\"F24\",\"F25\",\"F26\"],\"verification_points\":[\"确认优惠码折扣行为是否由替代规则覆盖\",\"如确认删除，按停用候选提交评审，不直接推断已生效或全面停用\"]}]},{\"rule_ref\":\"R3\",\"case_impacts\":[{\"case_ref\":\"C1\",\"level\":\"none\",\"reason\":\"新增订单导出接口规则与该用例现有验证目标及步骤无关，不产生直接影响。\",\"citations\":[\"F6\",\"F23\"],\"verification_points\":[]}]}],\"evidence_outcomes\":[],\"summary\":\"已完成用例C1对规则R1、R2、R3的影响分析：R2删除优惠码规则直接影响该用例，标记为重大影响并建议停用候选；R1与R3与该用例验证目标无关。\",\"unresolved\":[\"目标发布/部署状态仅有用户声明，缺少部署证据；R2/R3的实际生效状态未知。\",\"R2删除后未提供替代规则；仅提出停用候选，不做全面停用项目推断。\",\"用例执行说明提示存在刻意缺失的负向条件，现有证据不足以推断其具体内容，需保留待评审确认。\"]}","tool_calls":[]}